window.docContents[63].resolve({"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L5-___-The-oscillation-dies-out--Synopsis--Errors-prevented":{"contents":"* Similar names, different kinds: PhysLib's damping constant γ (kg/s) used as ISO's damping coefficient δ (s⁻¹) (HCP.L5_Damping#kinds_and_decay_rate).* Same dimension, different kind: δ + ω₀, which dimensions alone accept (HCP.L5_Damping#same_dimension_different_kinds).* Cross-system contamination: oscillator B's mass used in oscillator A's δ (HCP.L5_Damping#kinds_and_decay_rate).\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols\u0009L5 — The oscillation dies out\u0009Synopsis","header":"5.6.1.4. Errors prevented","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L5-___-The-oscillation-dies-out--Synopsis--Errors-prevented"}});